From eef3cfe435d0bf37a2b70e9f12c987e16f8dab19 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:46:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Disable Avalanche by default for Lotus V1

The Lotus V1 network does not run Avalanche, but the rebased node kept
eCash's defaults: -avalanche, -avalanchepreconsensus and
-avalanchepreconsensusmining were all enabled. With those defaults,
CreateNewBlock selects addFinalizedTxs, which mines only
Avalanche-finalized transactions, whenever preconsensus is active. Lotus
templates currently stay non-empty only because the pinned base also
requires an Avalanche-finalized tip before preconsensus activates, and
Lotus never has one. Default node behavior should not depend on that
indirect condition.

Default all three options to off. Block templates then always use the
custom fee-based assembler from patch 001 unless an operator explicitly
opts in. The Avalanche implementation, its RPCs and the explicit
-avalanche=1, -avalanchepreconsensus=1 and -avalanchepreconsensusmining=1
paths are retained unchanged. With Avalanche off, the inherited upstream
logic also defaults -automaticunparking on and no longer advertises the
Avalanche service or opens Avalanche connections. Staking preconsensus
remains a separate option and has no effect while Avalanche is disabled.

The new miner_tests regression attaches an Avalanche processor, marks the
tip Avalanche-finalized, and assembles a block with node-configured
options, without overriding add_finalized_txs. Before this change the
template omits the ordinary signed spend; afterwards the spend is mined
and leaves the mempool. A second case keeps explicit preconsensus mining
opt-in excluding unfinalized spends. The existing preconsensus validity
fixture now opts in explicitly so it keeps exercising the finalized path.

This is a node default and mining-policy change, not a consensus change.
Inherited eCash functional tests that assume Avalanche is enabled by
default were not updated and are not part of the maintained V1 checks.

diff --git a/src/avalanche/avalanche.h b/src/avalanche/avalanche.h
index e99e9185ae78c41b00d56b175012286c9050e18d..aa147847af87c5fa78b15bf28559dd8485cc8ede 100644
--- a/src/avalanche/avalanche.h
+++ b/src/avalanche/avalanche.h
@@ -11,8 +11,12 @@
 
 /**
  * Is avalanche enabled by default.
+ *
+ * Lotus V1 does not run an Avalanche network, so the feature is disabled by
+ * default. The implementation remains available with an explicit
+ * -avalanche=1.
  */
-static constexpr bool AVALANCHE_DEFAULT_ENABLED = true;
+static constexpr bool AVALANCHE_DEFAULT_ENABLED = false;
 
 /**
  * Conflicting proofs cooldown time default value in seconds.
@@ -55,13 +59,20 @@ static constexpr double AVALANCHE_DEFAULT_MIN_AVAPROOFS_NODE_COUNT = 8;
 /** Default for -persistavapeers */
 static constexpr bool DEFAULT_PERSIST_AVAPEERS{true};
 
-/** Default for -avalanchepreconsensus */
-static constexpr bool DEFAULT_AVALANCHE_PRECONSENSUS{true};
+/**
+ * Default for -avalanchepreconsensus. Off for Lotus V1, which has no Avalanche
+ * transaction finalization; explicit opt-in remains available.
+ */
+static constexpr bool DEFAULT_AVALANCHE_PRECONSENSUS{false};
 
 /** Default for -avalanchestakingpreconsensus */
 static constexpr bool DEFAULT_AVALANCHE_STAKING_PRECONSENSUS{true};
 
-/** Default for -avalanchepreconsensusmining */
-static constexpr bool DEFAULT_AVALANCHE_MINING_PRECONSENSUS{true};
+/**
+ * Default for -avalanchepreconsensusmining. Off for Lotus V1 so block
+ * templates use normal fee-based transaction selection instead of mining only
+ * Avalanche-finalized transactions.
+ */
+static constexpr bool DEFAULT_AVALANCHE_MINING_PRECONSENSUS{false};
 
 #endif // BITCOIN_AVALANCHE_AVALANCHE_H
